      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstdint>\n#include <climits>\n#include <omp.h>\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n\nstatic inline int read_int() {\n    int x = 0;\n    char c = getchar_unlocked();\n    while (c <= ' ') c = getchar_unlocked();\n    bool neg = false;\n    if (c == '-') { neg = true; c = getchar_unlocked(); }\n    while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n        x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n        c = getchar_unlocked();\n    }\n    return neg ? -x : x;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = read_int();\n    int s = read_int();\n\n    const int stride = n + 1;\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        int base = i * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            mat[base + j] = read_int();\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::vector<int64_t> pref(static_cast<std::size_t>(stride) * static_cast<std::size_t>(stride), 0);\n\n    // Horizontal pass: cumulative sums per row\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        int64_t row_sum = 0;\n        int base_i = (i + 1) * stride;\n        int mat_base = i * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row_sum += mat[mat_base + j];\n            pref[base_i + (j + 1)] = row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Vertical pass: accumulate columns to complete integral image\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        const int64_t *prev_row = &pref[i * stride];\n        int64_t *cur_row = &pref[(i + 1) * stride];\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            cur_row[j + 1] += prev_row[j + 1];\n        }\n    }\n\n    int64_t mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n\n#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        const int base_i_ps = i * stride;\n        const int base_is_ps = (i + s) * stride;\n\n        // Process two columns at once using NEON\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 1 <= n - s; j += 2) {\n            int64x2_t v_a = vld1q_s64(&pref[base_is_ps + j + s]);\n            int64x2_t v_b = vld1q_s64(&pref[base_i_ps + j + s]);\n            int64x2_t v_c = vld1q_s64(&pref[base_is_ps + j]);\n            int64x2_t v_d = vld1q_s64(&pref[base_i_ps + j]);\n\n            int64x2_t v_sum = vsubq_s64(v_a, v_b);\n            v_sum = vsubq_s64(v_sum, v_c);\n            v_sum = vaddq_s64(v_sum, v_d);\n\n            const int64_t sum0 = vgetq_lane_s64(v_sum, 0);\n            const int64_t sum1 = vgetq_lane_s64(v_sum, 1);\n            if (sum0 > mxSum) mxSum = sum0;\n            if (sum1 > mxSum) mxSum = sum1;\n        }\n\n        // Handle remaining column if odd number of columns\n        for (; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n            const int64_t sub_sum = pref[base_is_ps + j + s]\n                                  - pref[base_i_ps + j + s]\n                                  - pref[base_is_ps + j]\n                                  + pref[base_i_ps + j];\n            if (sub_sum > mxSum) mxSum = sub_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", static_cast<int>(mxSum));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Integrating fast integer input (A), flattened contiguous storage and two-pass integral image construction (A), OpenMP parallel reduction over rows with schedule(static) (B,C), and ARM NEON SIMD vectorization of submatrix sum computation (B) yields a correct, high-performance solution on the target ARM64 platform. The algorithm change to summed-area table is retained through the integral image approach.",
  "notes": "Combined best aspects from sources A, B, C: used flattened storage and two-pass integral image from A for memory efficiency; added OpenMP parallelism with static scheduling (from B/C) over rows; applied NEON vectorization as in B but using int64_t consistently to avoid type mismatch. Avoided collapse(2) because it conflicts with inner-loop vectorization.",
